# 1. An agent's file on main sets its session.

# Given: a project whose main holds an audit file naming its prompt, tools, model, effort and advisor, and an
# approved spec.
# When: the developer queues the spec and runs kiln.
# Between the two, a commit to main changes the audit's file. The build runs with the file it was queued with.
exec kiln queue x
cp _given/later-audit.md .kiln/agents/audit.md
exec git commit --quiet -am 'docs: change the audit after the queue'
exec kiln run
stdout '^x: landed on main'

# Then: the audit runs with that file's prompt,
! grep 'Find nothing' .claude-calls/audit/1/1/system
grep '\AAudit as this project does: read each package twice\.\n\n## kiln''s contract\n' .claude-calls/audit/1/1/system

# tools, model, effort
grep '^--tools\nRead,Grep$' .claude-calls/audit/1/1/args
grep '^--model\nsonnet$' .claude-calls/audit/1/1/args
grep '^--effort\nmax$' .claude-calls/audit/1/1/args

# and advisor.
grep '"advisorModel": "haiku"' .claude-calls/audit/1/1/settings.json

# The build agent's file names none of them, so it runs as every session ran before: every tool, Opus at medium
# effort, with Fable as its advisor.
! grep '^--tools$' .claude-calls/build/1/1/args
grep '^--model\nopus$' .claude-calls/build/1/1/args
grep '^--effort\nmedium$' .claude-calls/build/1/1/args
grep '"advisorModel": "fable"' .claude-calls/build/1/1/settings.json

-- .kiln/kiln.json --
{"gate": ["go vet ./...", "go test ./..."], "rounds": 1}
-- .kiln/agents/build.md --
Build the spec.
-- .kiln/agents/audit.md --
---
name: audit
description: The project's own audit, which a Claude Code subagent may run too.
tools: Read, Grep
model: sonnet
effort: max
advisor: haiku
---

Audit as this project does: read each package twice.
-- _given/later-audit.md --
---
model: opus
effort: low
advisor: fable
---

Find nothing.
-- claude.json --
{
  "build": {"1": {"1": [
    {"tool": {"name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "cp -R \"$WORK/_given/x/.\" ."}}},
    {"result": {"result": "Built x."}}
  ]}},
  "audit": {"1": {"1": [
    {"tool": {"name": "Read", "input": {"file_path": "x.go"}}},
    {"result": {"result": "read 2 packages, found 0"}}
  ]}}
}
-- go.mod --
module example.com/scratch

go 1.27
-- .kiln/specs/x.md --
# Spec 1: x

Status: Approved, 2026-11-10

## Overview

## Goals

## Non-goals

## Open Questions

## Acceptance tests

### 1. X answers

- **Given**: nothing.
- **When**: X is called.
- **Then**: it answers 42.

## Technical Plan

## Alternatives Considered
-- _given/x/x.go --
// Package scratch is where kiln's builds land.
package scratch

// X answers 42.
func X() int { return 42 }
-- _given/x/acceptance/x/x_test.go --
package x_test

import (
	"testing"

	"example.com/scratch"
)

func TestAT1(t *testing.T) {
	if got := scratch.X(); got != 42 {
		t.Fatalf("X answers %d, want 42", got)
	}
}
